Vulnerability Details
Type: Insufficient Session Expiration / Improper Session Invalidation
CWE: CWE-613 (Insufficient Session Expiration)
Affected endpoint(s): [account details page URL] and [cart/add-to-cart endpoint URL]
Steps to Reproduce
Create an account on bose.com (Account A).
Log in to Account A in a browser.
Open Burp Suite, enable Intercept, and capture an authenticated request to the account details page (e.g., GET [target.com]) containing the session cookie.
Send this request to Burp Repeater.
In the browser, click Logout on bose.com. Confirm the UI redirects to the login page / shows a logged-out state.
Return to Burp Repeater. Without modifying the previously captured session cookie, click Send again on the same request.
Observed result: The response still returns Account A's full authenticated data (name, email, address, saved card details), as if the session were still active — despite having logged out in step 5.
Additionally tested the add-to-cart endpoint (Target.com) the same way — cart modification also succeeded using the "logged out" cookie.
All submissions are subject to the Bose Privacy Policy
Impact
A session token captured before logout remains permanently (or indefinitely) usable.
Anyone who obtains a victim's cookie (public/shared computer, browser history sync, stolen device, network-level capture, malicious browser extension, etc.) retains full access to the account even after the victim logs out believing they are safe.
Exposed data includes PII (name, email, address) and payment method details, plus the ability to modify cart contents.
This defeats the entire security purpose of the "Logout" feature.
